WEBVTT

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.280
So one question about translation.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.060
Fir'own was not an Arab,

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.600
but he speaks in Arabic in the Qur'an.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.620
Musa was not an Arab but he speaks in Arabic in the Qur'an. 'Isa is not an Arab

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.060
but he speaks in Arabic in the Qur'an.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.960
Nuh 'alaihissalam we don't even know what he spoke.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.360
But he speaks in Arabic in the Qur'an.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.250
Okay. Ibrahim 'alaihissalam traveled all over the place.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.990
He traveled in Iraq. He traveled in Palestine. He traveled all over.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.360
We don't know what he spoke, but he spoke Arabic in

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.560
the Qur'an. Which means Allah is translating isn't He?

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:40.750
Allah is translating.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.060
So you ever heard this concept of lost in translation?

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.010
Some things are lost in translation because

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.660
no one language can fully be communicated in

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:56.300
another language. At least not when human beings translate.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:59.760
But the idea of the Qur'an is that Allah is translating.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.560
And so there's a fundamental difference between us

00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:07.490
attempting to translate and Allah translating.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.360
Allah's translation, by definition, would have to be perfect.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:15.000
And a perfect translation means that not only are the words translated,

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:19.210
but the emotions and the environment and the the feeling.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.560
The complete scene that took place is translated,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.710
so the translations of the Qur'an actually go far beyond the words that were said

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:31.950
originally. They capture the words, but they actually also capture the emotions

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.360
of the original people who said them.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.550
This is what makes the translations of the Qur'an themselves miraculous.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.390
Also,

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.300
this teaches us a lesson that we have to exhaust great deals of

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:47.550
effort in trying to translate the word of Allah to anyone else,

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:50.740
because Allah Himself left us the legacy of translation.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.250
One of the most beautiful examples of translation

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.260
is by Salman al-Farsi.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.350
You guys better know who that is.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.350
Salman al-Farsi

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.860
who translated the Fatiha into Farsi.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.750
He translated--he actually wrote a translation of the Fatiha in Persian.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:11.110
And to this day, any translation of the Qur'an in Persian.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.530
The translation of the Fatiha has never changed.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.660
It's the same one. It is from Salman al-Farsi.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.560
So the legacy of translating the Qur'an begins with the Sahaba,

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.050
and the legacy of translating the past is in the Qur'an itself.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.670
The Qur'an itself translated other cultures into the Arabic language, right?

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.360
So there

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.600
is that that that issue.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.860
So, yes, there are, for example, and there are other issues associated with this.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.950
For example, Allah will say sometimes

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.860
you know that the angels came to Zakariyya and said,

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.290
'You will not speak for three days.'

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.760
Another time they'll say, 'You will not speak for three nights.'

00:02:42.914 --> 00:02:45.380
 Wait a second and in Surat al-'Imran

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:48.513
Allah said, 'You won't speak for three days.' In another--in Surat Mariam

00:02:48.545 --> 00:02:50.169
Allah says he won't speak for three nights

00:02:50.217 --> 00:02:53.150
أَلَّا تُكَلِّمَ ٱلنَّاسَ ثَلَٰثَ لَيَالٍۢ سَوِيًّا

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:57.280
And there ( ثَلَٰثَةَ أَيَّامٍ إِلَّا رَمْزًا) 
How come? It's the same conversation

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.050
how come three days and three nights? Well, really interestingly,

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:03.460
you know, is it possible that the angels repeated themselves?

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:08.300
In the beginning of the conversation, they said, three days, remember? Three days.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.960
Okay. And as they're leaving, they say, what?

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.070
Three nights. But why separate those two?

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:15.790
He separated those two for yet another beautiful reason.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:20.650
Ali 'Imran is full of evidence and bringing people out of darkness into light and

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:24.600
taking things that were secret and making them known and there Allah used three days,

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.460
because the the idea of bringing things out of the

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:32.910
darkness into light and removing secrecy is associated with the day.

00:03:32.966 --> 00:03:37.808
And in Surat Mariam the entire Surah the first passage of the Surah is dark.

00:03:37.848 --> 00:03:41.660
Zakariyya 'alaihissalam is in the middle of the night. He's asking Allah secretly for a Du'a.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:45.800
He's telling Allah, he's reached old age and the hair has lost color.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:49.160
It's been it's gone on fire. And everything is dark.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.390
And still. And I'm about to die and people are going to take my place,

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:54.810
and I don't know what's going to happen.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:59.120
So the dark texture of Surat Mariam's beginning is complemented

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:02.340
by saying, 'You won't speak to people for three nights.'

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.390
In other words, the Qur'an actually takes into account

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.360
what kind of mood is the passage

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:07.550
generating.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:10.770
And the wording of the Ayat is actually, you know,

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.140
influenced by the mood of the passage.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:14.720
It's consistent with it. Subhanallah.

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:18.130
There's another-- just a literary nuance inside the Qur'an.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.750
This next example that I want to share with you now

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.490
is a really, really beautiful example.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:27.120
It is a summary of the life of the Prophet ﷺ.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:28.790
And I'll show you how.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:29.474
Listen carefully,

00:04:29.506 --> 00:04:34.103
أَنزَلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءً 
Allah sent- He sent sent water down from the sky

00:04:34.143 --> 00:04:36.741
فَسَالَتْ أَوْدِيَةٌۢ بِقَدَرِهَاً

00:04:36.821 --> 00:04:39.340
then the valley--listen. Water came from the sky.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.850
Means it started raining right?

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.383
فَسَالَتْ أَوْدِيَةٌۢ بِقَدَرِهَا

00:04:43.423 --> 00:04:46.930
Then the valleys started getting flooded as much

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.970
as they possibly could. (بِقَدَرِهَا) as much as they could.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.860
So Allah is describing rain, and it rained so much that it

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.530
floods. Okay.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:58.860
فَٱحْتَمَلَ ٱلسَّيْلُ زَبَدًا رَّابِيًا
 Then the floodwaters

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:02.360
they started carrying the foam. You know what foam means?

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:06.660
Foam (زَبَدًا) is like, uh, you know, when you have on the ground, you have, uh,

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:11.610
torn up pieces of leaves and twigs and small rocks and pebbles and things like that?

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.750
Just this--just the stuff on the ground.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:17.370
And when the water comes, it starts kind of sweeping all of that up

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.260
and it turns into foam on top.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.160
So the flood waters start taking the dirt and

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.940
the filth and the impurities of the land.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:28.210
It starts flooding them away and turning them into to foam.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:32.590
Uh, so now, speaking of foam, this bubbly stuff, this foam.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:34.926
Speaking of it, there's another kind of foam.

00:05:34.982 --> 00:05:39.860
وَمِمَّا يُوقِدُونَ عَلَيْهِ فِى ٱلنَّارِ
And you know, additionally

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:45.650
there's another kind of foam that comes when you light-- when you

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:49.150
when you light fires up, in order to burn metals.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:51.930
So there's a quick transition in the Ayah.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:56.830
First Allah talks about rainwater and valleys being flooded and foam coming

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:59.210
and the filth being removed in the form of foam.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:00.410
Speaking of foam,

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.030
you can imagine another kind of foam when you burn iron or

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:07.830
you burn steel and you burn gold and the foam rises,

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:10.880
the bubbles rise to the top and He says, 'Why do you burn it?'

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:18.000
ٱبْتِغَآءَ حِلْيَةٍ أَوْ مَتَٰعٍۢ
 And in the pursuit of jewelry or in the pursuit of utensils.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.790
In other words, when do you burn metal?

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:23.500
When you burn metal, when you want to mold it to make jewelry or you burn metal

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:26.260
to make a fork and a spoon and a shovel or something,

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:26.960
you understand?

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.286
And so He says
زَبَدٌ مِّثْلُهُۥ

00:06:29.311 --> 00:06:34.050
Actually that is another kind of foam similar to the previous foam,

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.650
similar to the previous (زَبَدٌ مِّثْلُهُۥ)

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.486
كَذَٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْحَقَّ وَٱلْبَٰطِلَ

00:06:40.557 --> 00:06:46.159
 That is how Allah strikes truth against falsehood.
فَأَمَّا ٱلزَّبَدُ فَيَذْهَبُ جُفَآءً

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:50.860
And as far as the original foam, it will dissipate. It will disappear.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:56.100
It will wither away. It will become nothing.
وَأَمَّا مَا يَنفَعُ ٱلنَّاسَ فَيَمْكُثُ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ

00:06:56.340 --> 00:07:00.150
As far as what benefits people, it will become stationed in the earth

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:02.446
كَذَٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْأَمْثَالَ

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:06.230
That is how Allah gives examples. Wow, it seems

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:11.740
at first glance, it is a very confusing example. Floodwaters came, foam rose.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:15.540
People are melting metals, foam rises by the way,

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.750
they melt metals to make jewelry and they melt metals to make utensils.

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:23.550
And then Allah strikes truth against falsehood.

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:27.560
Then the foam will disappear. And what benefits people will stay in place.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:30.642
And that's the example
Allah gives. Let's explore this a little furhter.

00:07:30.682 --> 00:07:32.900
The Qur'an came from the sky.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:36.630
It came into the valley of Makkah and it flooded every street.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.750
Every house. Just like the rain comes from the sky and the water floods

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.350
as much as it possibly can.

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:46.650
Now there are people in Makkah who internalize the message of Islam.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:50.260
The water enters the soil and benefits the soil.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.580
Life comes out of the soil when water enters.

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:57.240
But there are elements of the soil that are useless, that are lifeless,

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.720
that have no good in them.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.560
They are simply the dirt of the earth, the filth of the earth.

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:04.140
It gets flooded away and moved out of the place.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:06.480
So Allah is describing by flood,

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:09.730
the flood waters here represent the message of Islam, the Qur'an.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:16.760
The filth that rose to the top is the disbelievers who rejected the message of Islam.

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:21.250
And they have clearly been separated from the believers,

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:26.310
He says, speaking of this separation, there's another kind of separation.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:27.650
When you burn metal,

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:32.240
the Prophet ﷺ moves to Medina.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:37.380
If the filth, the foam, the filth of Makkah was the disbelievers,

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:39.159
what is the filth of Medina?

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:41.960
What is the filth of Medina?

00:08:43.039 --> 00:08:46.760
I'll give you a hint. It's deeply embedded inside the metal.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:49.550
It's the hypocrites.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.960
And in order to get those hypocrites out, what must you do?

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:54.860
You remember the parable that was given before.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:09:00.660
You must burn the metal, and in order to burn the metal, the foam will rise.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:02.260
But why do you burn the metal?

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.860
What does Allah say? Why do you burn the medal?

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:07.560
To make jewelry and to make

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.070
utensils. An example of jewelry would be a necklace.

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:12.950
Bangles.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:14.840
Right? Bracelets.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:19.340
Those would be jewelry. What would be an example of a utensil? A fork, a spoon.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:19.860
Right?

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:23.920
Now, you tell me if you're gonna make all the effort to burn metal,

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:25.660
which one would you rather get at the end?

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:29.010
I mean, they're both useful, but which one is more valuable?

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.120
Jewelry. Which is why He mentioned jewelry first.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.530
Interestingly, I already told you before

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:38.660
Muslims being put under intense temperatures, what was that used for?

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:43.350
That was that was an imagery of the Qur'an for battle. Remember?

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:46.760
That's the Quranic imagery for battle. Now,

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:48.870
when the Muslims go into battle,

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.170
when the Sahaba go into Badr, when they go into Uhud

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.340
when they go into Ahzaab,

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:55.064
why do they go into Badr, Uhud and Ahzaab?

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:56.550
For what reason?

00:09:57.640 --> 00:09:59.380
What are they--what are they running towards?

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:01.150
What do they want?

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:02.960
One answer. They want Jannah.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.360
Simple answer. They want

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:09.160
Jannah. In Surat as-Saff however Allah says you want Jannah,

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:11.360
but you also want victory.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:17.130
You want Jannah and you also want victory. And as a matter of fact, He says in

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.267
Surat as-Saff He say hello to look

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:22.750
هَلْ أَدُلُّكُمْ عَلَىٰ تِجَٰرَةٍۢ تُنجِيكُم مِّنْ عَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍۢ

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:26.240
Should I tell you of a deal,

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.740
of a business deal that will save you from painful punishment?

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:31.093
And if you take this deal you know,

00:10:31.231 --> 00:10:34.910
يَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ ذُنُوبَكُمْ وَيُدْخِلْكُمْ جَنَّٰتٍۢ تَجْرِى مِن تَحْتِهَا ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُ

00:10:34.957 --> 00:10:39.460
وَمَسَٰكِنَ طَيِّبَةً فِى جَنَّٰتِ عَدْنٍۢ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلْفَوْزُ ٱلْعَظِيمُ

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:43.960
I will enter you into gardens. You'll have beautiful homes.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.760
You're going to be really, really happy there.

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:49.160
That's the ultimate success.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.580
When you're living in the gardens of Eden.

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:53.650
وَأُخْرَىٰ تُحِبُّونَهَا

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:58.930
Secondarily you also love that help of Allah would come and victory should arrive.

00:10:58.967 --> 00:11:01.070
نَصْرٌ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَفَتْحٌ قَرِيبٌ

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:05.950
In other words, there are two goals. The first goal is Jannah. The second goal is what?

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.910
Victory. The first goal is far more valuable than the second. Why?

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:11.200
Because the first goal is Jannah,

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.930
and the second goal is just in this world; victory in this world.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.380
Now, in this Ayah, when you burn metal,

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:19.450
you burn it for something far more valuable and far less valuable.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:23.610
The far more valuable is jewelry. The far less valuable is

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.450
utensils, but they're still good.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:29.580
But just don't be so impressed with utensils. At the end of the day you just use them.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:32.360
You're not there--You're like you don't-You are not proud of your utensils.

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:37.170
Utensils aren't of real value.
What's the real value? Your jewelry.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:40.220
So if you have to let go of the utensils or jewelry if you're like hey,

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:41.290
we have to leave here.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.130
Make sure you pack all the valuables.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.460
What are you gonna pack?

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:48.660
The jewelry. 'Oh, wait. I forgot my fork.' You're not gonna do that.

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:51.640
You're not gonna do that. So what is the Muslim learning?

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:54.390
We are working towards Jannah. If victory comes, that's cool.

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:56.260
If not, it's not a big deal. We still got Jannah.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:57.360
Right?

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:00.650
Now look at this example. This incredible example.

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:04.960
The first kind of foam came as a result of a flood.

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:08.320
The second kind of foam came as a result of burning fire.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:13.350
Just like that the Makkan Qur'an, the D'awah of Islam spread everywhere.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:16.250
And it was easy to separate believer from disbeliever.

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:21.680
But the separation of the Munafiq from the Mu'min in Medina could only happen when

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:25.490
Muslims went into battle. And Muslims only went into battle to earn the gold,

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:26.150
which is

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:30.460
Jannah. And also maybe hopefully get the spoon, which is

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:32.160
victory.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:36.060
This is how Allah strikes truth against falsehood.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:40.310
Then Allah goes back and He says, 'Let me tell you about the first foam.'

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:42.750
The first foam was from the flood. You remember that?

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:48.160
The foam from the flood, who does it represent? The Quraysh.

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:50.060
The Quraysh of Makkah.

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:52.550
The second form who does it represent?

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:53.920
The hypocrites.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:55.982
Allah only talks about the first foam and He says

00:12:56.022 --> 00:12:59.240
فَأَمَّا ٱلزَّبَدُ فَيَذْهَبُ جُفَآءً

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:03.260
As for the first foam, it will go and dissipate and disappear.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:05.650
What happened eventually in Makkah?

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:08.350
Did the Kuffar of Makkah disappear?

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:11.250
Did Kufr disappear from Makkah? Sure.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:13.390
Interestingly enough, in this,

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.850
Ayah Allah did not talk about the disappearance of the second kind of foam.

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:18.760
What was the second kind of foam?

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:22.350
Hypocrisy. Did hypocrisy disappear from the Ummah?

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:23.250
No.

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:25.606
And then at the end of it all,

00:13:25.646 --> 00:13:29.208
وَأَمَّا مَا يَنفَعُ ٱلنَّاسَ فَيَمْكُثُ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:32.120
And as for what will benefit people, it will stay in the land.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:34.250
In other words, the word of Allah is established.

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:37.430
It has entered and penetrated and the word of Allah

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:39.770
and the Qur'an And this Deen will continue to spread.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:42.260
It has now become a part of this land.

00:13:43.131 --> 00:13:46.260
So (فَيَمْكُثُ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ) and then at the end of it all Allah says

00:13:46.293 --> 00:13:48.590
And that is how Allah gives an example.

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.560
Incredible stuff.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.360
Just so you know why this is so powerful?

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:02.250
Because the next time the believer sees rain, he remembers the entire Seerah.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.350
He just remembers the entire Seerah.

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:10.360
Also, by giving the example of the message of Islam spreading to every valley.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.440
We are learning a very powerful philosophical lesson about

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:16.050
how Islam should be carried to the world today.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.504
And that lesson is as follows.

00:14:18.599 --> 00:14:23.860
Unless the message of the Qur'an enters every nook and cranny.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:29.450
Unless every household in society knows what the Qur'an has to say,

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:32.260
we cannot blame the disbelievers.

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:37.360
We cannot take the next step and say we have to go to war against the disbelievers.

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:41.030
Because the Prophet ﷺ did not pick up

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:44.460
arms against the Quraysh until they actually fully what?

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:47.810
Knew. We are living in complicated times.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.990
We are in such complicated times forget telling the most

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.760
non Muslim world about the message of the Qur'an.

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:59.310
We are living in the tragic times where the Muslims don't know the word of Allah.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:03.740
So what are we talking about the next steps for? What was the actual mission of

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:06.960
the Prophet ﷺ? To deliver this message.

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:10.600
Today we're not even doing the delivery to our own families.

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:13.160
So how are we talking about the next steps?

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:18.300
There's a loss of perspective that's that's, you know, that's afflicting us.